<urn:atm:triage:finding/AXPE-QA-114>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AXPE-QA-114" ;
  triage:title "No mechanical guard against the task projection SQL bodies drifting apart" ;
  triage:description "After AXPE-QA-103, task_sql.rs and task_ledger_reader.rs each own a SELECT statement over tasks/task_events built from the shared TASK_COLUMNS/TASK_EVENT_COLUMNS constants. The self-test task_projection_column_lists_have_one_crate_owner only checks that the column-list constants are declared once; nothing catches the two SQL statement bodies (WHERE/ORDER BY shape) silently diverging on a future schema change. Remediation: add a unit test in atm-storage-rusqlite that asserts the reader's statements are built from the shared constants and match the task_sql shape (e.g. compare the rendered SQL text of both paths against one canonical template), or fold the shape into a shared const fn that both call; no boundary relaxation, no new crate edge." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
  triage:triageMode "phase_end_review" ;
